ild/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/epic.md:196:**AC-2.2:** Version-level provenance identifies which process produced each\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/epic.md:199:- **TC-2.2a: Producing process recorded on version**\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/epic.md:203:- **TC-2.2b: Earlier version provenance remains readable**\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/epic.md:208:**AC-2.3:** Current artifact summaries resolve the latest version correctly\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/epic.md:211:- **TC-2.3a: Latest version shown after later process revision**\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/epic.md:215:- **TC-2.3b: Earlier versions remain reviewable**\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/epic.md:503:| currentVersionLabel | string | no | non-empty when present | Latest current version label |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/epic.md:512:| currentVersionLabel | string | no | non-empty when present | Latest current version label for the artifact |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/epic.md:523:| producedByProcessId | string | yes | non-empty | Process that created this version |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/epic.md:636:### Story 2: Versioned Checkpoint Realignment\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/epic.md:643:- AC-2.1\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/epic.md:644:- AC-2.2\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/epic.md:645:- AC-2.3\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design-server.md:19:- process provenance lives on `artifactVersions.createdByProcessId`\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design-server.md:62:| Artifacts | **Schema migration**: `artifacts` table trims to project-scoped identity (`projectId`, `displayName`, new `createdAt`). Removed: `processId`, `contentStorageId`, `currentVersionLabel`, `updatedAt` — version-specific state relocates to or is derived from `artifactVersions`, and process linkage moves to process-reference / provenance surfaces. Epic 3's checkpoint writer is rewritten to insert a new `artifactVersions` row rather than overwrite in place |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design-server.md:84:│   │       └── materials-section.reader.ts                   # MODIFIED (artifact summary derives currentVersionLabel + updatedAt from artifactVersions)\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design-server.md:135:├── artifactVersions.ts                                       # NEW\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design-server.md:157:| `platform-store.ts` | MODIFIED | Add durable reads for `artifactVersions`, `packageSnapshots`, `packageSnapshotMembers`; add `getArtifactVersionContentUrl` + `getLatestArtifactVersion` helpers; add `insertArtifactVersion` and `publishPackageSnapshot` typed write wrappers; **rewrite any existing call site that reads `artifacts.contentStorageId` or artifact-row process ownership** to use `getLatestArtifactVersion` plus process-reference state; extend shell `availableActions` projections (multiple sites) to consult reviewability when including `'review'` | Convex functions, reviewability check | AC-1 through AC-6 |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design-server.md:158:| `materials-section.reader.ts` | MODIFIED | Artifact summary read-path rewrite — derive `currentVersionLabel` and `updatedAt` from `artifactVersions[latest]` via `getLatestArtifactVersion`. `ArtifactSummary` schema unchanged; derivation logic is the change | `PlatformStore` | AC-2 |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design-server.md:165:| `convex/artifactVersions.ts` | NEW | Durable per-artifact version rows (content pointer lives here after the storage model change); typed `internalMutation insertArtifactVersion`; `internalQuery` list / get / content-URL | Convex schema + typed functions | AC-2, AC-6 |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design-server.md:168:| `convex/artifacts.ts` | **MODIFIED (storage model change)** | Table shape trims to three fields: `projectId` (kept), `displayName` (kept), `createdAt` (new). **Removed: `processId`, `contentStorageId`, `currentVersionLabel`, `updatedAt`.** Rewrite Epic 3's checkpoint writer path to call `insertArtifactVersion` instead of overwriting the artifact row. Update every caller of the removed fields to use `getLatestArtifactVersion` plus process-reference state where needed. See §Artifact Storage Model Change for the field-by-field delta and read-path implications for callers like `materials-section.reader.ts`. | AC-2 |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design-server.md:220:Reduce the `artifacts` row to generic identity only. Epic 3's closure chunks landed `contentStorageId` on `artifacts` as the content pointer; Epic 4 removes that field and relocates the pointer to a new `artifactVersions` table. This is Shape A from the decision record — a single source of truth for \"current artifact content\" (the latest row in `artifactVersions`) rather than a denormalized field that write paths have to keep in sync.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design-server.md:222:A process that rapidly iterates on an artifact (say, 50 revisions across a work session) produces 50 `artifactVersions` rows — one per revision. That is exactly what a chronological history table is for. An embedded array on the `artifacts` row would concentrate per-revision churn on a shared identity row and tile the 1 MB per-row ceiling; a separate table is the standard Convex pattern and what the guidelines require.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design-server.md:226:Content itself lives in Convex File Storage. `artifactVersions.contentStorageId` is the pointer; the row does not hold the bytes. This preserves Epic 3's decision that artifact content lives in File Storage rather than inline in Convex documents (to avoid the 1 MB per-row ceiling); only the location of the pointer changes.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design-server.md:228:Package snapshots are **immutable after publication**. The `publishPackageSnapshot` mutation writes the snapshot row and all member rows in one transaction. There is no \"update a snapshot after the fact\" path in Epic 4. Revising an artifact produces a new `artifactVersions` row; publishing a new package produces a new `packageSnapshots` row. This immutability is what makes \"the published package still points at the same member versions\" a structural property rather than a runtime check.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design-server.md:236:Epic 4 trims the `artifacts` table to project-scoped identity only, relocates all version-specific state to the new `artifactVersions` table, and rewrites Epic 3's checkpoint writer path. The work lands in Chunk 0 (schema change) + Chunk 2 (write-path rewrite and read-path rewrite).\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design-server.md:246:Everything else about an artifact — what version is current, where content lives, when it was last updated — is derived from `artifactVersions` at read time.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design-server.md:257:| `currentVersionLabel` | `v.union(v.string(), v.null())` | **REMOVED** | Derived at read time from `artifactVersions[latest].versionLabel`; `null` when no versions exist |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design-server.md:258:| `contentStorageId` | `v.id('_storage')` | **REMOVED** | Moved to `artifactVersions.contentStorageId`; one row per revision |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design-server.md:259:| `updatedAt` | `v.string()` | **REMOVED** | Derived at read time from `artifactVersions[latest].createdAt`, falling back to `artifacts.createdAt` when no versions exist |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design-server.md:272:Three fields, all project-scoped identity. No version-specific state. Existing indexes on `artifacts` (notably `by_projectId_updatedAt`) need attention: `updatedAt` is no longer on the row, so queries that previously sorted artifacts by `updatedAt` must either sort by `artifacts.createdAt` (identity-level recency) or join against `artifactVersions` for true latest-activity ordering. Both options are acceptable for the first cut; the read-path rewrite documents which choice each call site makes.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design-server.md:278:| Checkpoint writer | Overwrites `artifacts.contentStorageId` on each revision | Calls `insertArtifactVersion` to append a new `artifactVersions` row; does not touch `artifacts` |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design-server.md:280:| Latest version label | Read `artifacts.currentVersionLabel` | `getLatestArtifactVersion(artifactId).versionLabel` |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design-server.md:282:| Orphaned blobs on revision | Old blob was orphaned | Every revision's blob stays referenced by its `artifactVersions` row |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design-server.md:288:`ArtifactSummary` (from `apps/platform/shared/contracts/schemas.ts:143`) is the shape that shell and materials consumers see per-artifact. The schema **does not change** — it keeps `currentVersionLabel: string | null` and `updatedAt: string`. What changes is how those fields are *populated* after the storage model change. The `artifacts` row no longer carries these values as denormalized latest fields; instead they are derived at read time from the latest `artifactVersions` row.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design-server.md:294:| `currentVersionLabel` | From `artifacts.currentVersionLabel` | Derived from `artifactVersions[latest].versionLabel` for the artifact; `null` when no versions exist |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design-server.md:295:| `updatedAt` | From `artifacts.updatedAt` | Derived from `artifactVersions[latest].createdAt` for the artifact; falls back to the new `artifacts.createdAt` field when no versions exist |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design-server.md:299:- **`apps/platform/server/services/processes/readers/materials-section.reader.ts`** — MODIFIED. Today this reader produces `ArtifactSummary` rows for the process work surface's materials envelope. Epic 4 extends its per-artifact projection to `getLatestArtifactVersion(artifactId)` and derive `currentVersionLabel` + `updatedAt` from that row. When the materials projection returns N artifacts, this costs N version-lookups; at first-cut material-list scale (≤ 20 items per process in Epic 2's NFR) this is acceptable. If a future epic materializes much larger materials lists, denormalization can be reintroduced as a performance optimization.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design-server.md:300:- **`apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts`** — MODIFIED. Every call site that currently reads `artifacts.contentStorageId` or reads a denormalized `currentVersionLabel`/`updatedAt` off the `artifacts` row. The grep target is any reference to those three fields. Each site is rewritten to use `getLatestArtifactVersion` (a new `PlatformStore` method backed by the `by_artifactId_createdAt` Convex index).\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design-server.md:302:No denormalized latest-version cache stays on `artifacts`. Single source of truth = `artifactVersions`. This is the same decision that drove Shape A for the content pointer; the summary fields follow the same principle.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design-server.md:308:| `artifacts` | **MODIFIED (storage model change)** | Generic project-scoped artifact identity row after Epic 4: `projectId`, `displayName`, `createdAt` | `processId`, `contentStorageId`, `currentVersionLabel`, `updatedAt` are removed; all version-specific state moves to or is derived from `artifactVersions`; new `createdAt` field added for identity-level recency |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design-server.md:309:| `artifactVersions` | NEW | One row per durable version of one artifact; content via File Storage | Indexed by `artifactId` + `createdAt` |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design-server.md:317:#### `artifactVersions`\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design-server.md:325:export const artifactVersionsTableFields = {\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design-server.md:339:defineTable(artifactVersionsTableFields)\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design-server.md:373:  artifactVersionId: v.id('artifactVersions'),\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design-server.md:391:// convex/artifactVersions.ts\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design-server.md:403:    return await ctx.db.insert('artifactVersions', {\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design-server.md:419:  artifactVersionId: v.id('artifactVersions'),\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design-server.md:527:  currentVersionLabel?: string;\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design-server.md:857:| Convex state modules | `convex/artifactVersions.ts`, `convex/packageSnapshots.ts`, `convex/packageSnapshotMembers.ts` | Public/internal typed queries + the two typed write mutations (`insertArtifactVersion`, `publishPackageSnapshot`) |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design-server.md:881:**Covers:** AC-2.1, AC-2.2, AC-2.3, AC-2.4, AC-6.3 (body-render degradation)\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design-server.md:894:    Note over Browser,Renderer: AC-2.x\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design-server.md:928:| TC-2.1a | new revision becomes current | `tests/service/server/artifact-review-api.test.ts` | artifact with two versions | versions[0] is the newer; `isCurrent: true` |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design-server.md:929:| TC-2.1b | earlier revision remains reviewable | `tests/service/server/artifact-review-api.test.ts` | artifact with two versions, query ?versionId=older | selectedVersion is the older one |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design-server.md:930:| TC-2.2a | artifact identity visible | `tests/service/server/artifact-review-api.test.ts` | artifact target | artifactId + displayName present |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design-server.md:931:| TC-2.2b | version identity visible | `tests/service/server/artifact-review-api.test.ts` | any version | versionLabel on selectedVersion |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epic