v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/stories/02-start-or-resume-with-environment-preparation.md:58:**AC-2.2:** Environment preparation hydrates the process's current artifact references, current outputs, and already-attached current sources into the working copy before controlled work depends on them.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/stories/02-start-or-resume-with-environment-preparation.md:60:- **TC-2.2a: Current materials hydrate into environment**\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/stories/02-start-or-resume-with-environment-preparation.md:64:- **TC-2.2b: Process with partial working set still hydrates correctly**\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/stories/02-start-or-resume-with-environment-preparation.md:69:**AC-2.3:** The surface shows hydration progress and hydration failure as part of the environment state without requiring manual refresh.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/stories/02-start-or-resume-with-environment-preparation.md:71:- **TC-2.3a: Hydration progress becomes visible**\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/stories/02-start-or-resume-with-environment-preparation.md:75:- **TC-2.3b: Hydration failure becomes visible**\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/stories/02-start-or-resume-with-environment-preparation.md:80:**AC-2.4:** A process does not enter active running work until the required working set is ready or a recoverable failure state is shown.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/stories/02-start-or-resume-with-environment-preparation.md:82:- **TC-2.4a: Running begins after readiness**\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/stories/02-start-or-resume-with-environment-preparation.md:86:- **TC-2.4b: Running does not begin after failed preparation**\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/stories/02-start-or-resume-with-environment-preparation.md:91:**AC-2.5:** The process surface distinguishes read-only and writable attached sources before the process depends on code work against them.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/stories/02-start-or-resume-with-environment-preparation.md:93:- **TC-2.5a: Writable source is identifiable**\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/stories/02-start-or-resume-with-environment-preparation.md:97:- **TC-2.5b: Read-only source is identifiable**\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/03--process-environment-and-controlled-execution/stories/02-start-or-resume-with-environment-preparation.md:165:- Story tests cover TC-2.1a through TC-2.5b\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/stories/coherence-review.md:78:- **AC-2.4 zero-version reachability:** zero-version artifacts are not reviewable targets and are excluded from available target lists by Story 1. Story 2 AC-2.4 / TC-2.4a covers only the direct artifact URL case where an artifact identity is reached through an otherwise valid process review context despite having no durable versions. This resolves the apparent tension without changing reviewability rules.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/stories/coverage.md:16:| AC-2.1 | TC-2.1a, TC-2.1b | Story 2 | `convex/artifacts.test.ts` | Write path creates versions without reassigning artifact identity |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/stories/coverage.md:17:| AC-2.2 | TC-2.2a, TC-2.2b | Story 2 | `convex/artifacts.test.ts`; `tests/service/server/artifact-review-api.test.ts` | Version provenance remains visible across histories |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/stories/coverage.md:18:| AC-2.3 | TC-2.3a, TC-2.3b | Story 2 | `tests/service/server/project-shell-bootstrap-api.test.ts`; `tests/service/server/artifact-review-api.test.ts`; `tests/integration/review-workspace.test.ts` | Latest-version summaries and earlier-version reviewability |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/stories/coverage.md:24:| AC-4.2 | TC-4.2a, TC-4.2b, TC-4.2c | Story 4 | `convex/packageSnapshots.test.ts`; `convex/processPackageContexts.test.ts` | Current package-building context rule |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/stories/coverage.md:38:| Path 1.3 | Persist a later-process revision as a new version with visible provenance and updated latest-version summary | Story 2 | TC-2.1a, TC-2.2a, TC-2.3a | `convex/artifacts.test.ts`; `tests/service/server/project-shell-bootstrap-api.test.ts` |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/stories/coverage.md:41:| Path 2.1 | Seed a current package-building context from current refs and earlier pinned versions | Story 4 | TC-4.2a, TC-4.2c | `convex/processPackageContexts.test.ts` |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design.md:35:| Current Epic 3 artifact write path overwrites `artifacts.contentStorageId` rather than preserving prior revisions; AC-2.1 (\"earlier version remains available for review\") cannot be satisfied against that schema | `convex/artifacts.ts` (Epic 3 closure chunks); AC-2.1, AC-2.3 | **Shape A — direct schema change to Epic 3's artifacts table.** Trim `artifacts` to project-level identity only (`projectId`, `displayName`, new `createdAt`). Remove `processId`, `contentStorageId`, `currentVersionLabel`, and `updatedAt`. Version provenance lives on `artifactVersions.createdByProcessId`, and process reviewability is derived from process refs / pinned review context rather than artifact-row ownership. Single source of truth for \"current artifact content\" = `latest artifactVersions row by createdAt`. Epic 4 owns this storage model change because pre-customer stance in Epic 3's addendum permits direct schema edits (no user-data preservation required) and the removed fields have no long-term callers yet. | Resolved — deviated; later reinforced by Epic 5 alignment |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design.md:42:| Artifact summary migration (how `currentVersionLabel` and `updatedAt` on `ArtifactSummary` continue to work after `artifacts.contentStorageId` is dropped) was not explicit in the first revision | — (design drafting gap) | `ArtifactSummary` schema unchanged; fields derived at read time from `artifactVersions[latest]` via a new `getLatestArtifactVersion` helper on `PlatformStore`. `materials-section.reader.ts` MODIFIED to co-query version rows per artifact. No denormalized latest cache on `artifacts` | Resolved — clarified |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design.md:55:  (`artifactVersions.createdByProcessId`)\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design.md:79:The second posture change is durability. MDV treats documents as mutable local files. Liminal Build treats every artifact as a durable, versioned, project-level record with version-level process provenance. Epic 4 introduces two new durable concerns — `artifactVersions` as the versioned content pointer (one row per revision, each row pointing at its own Convex File Storage blob), and `packageSnapshots` plus `packageSnapshotMembers` as the durable, ordered, stable-forever record of what was published as one reviewable set. Epic 4 also modifies Epic 3's artifact schema: `contentStorageId`, `currentVersionLabel`, `updatedAt`, and the old artifact-level process attachment all come off the `artifacts` row, relocating to or being derived from `artifactVersions` or process-reference state. What remains on `artifacts` is project-scoped identity only (`projectId`, `displayName`, and a new `createdAt`). Epic 3's checkpoint path is updated to insert a new version row rather than overwrite in place. A package published today must still point at the same artifact versions after a member is revised tomorrow; that \"pinned at publication\" property is fundamental to review semantics and is expressed directly in the schema. Reviewability for a package requires at least one durable member at read time, and `publishPackageSnapshot` rejects zero-member publication input so the happy path never creates a memberless snapshot. Package membership is not constrained to artifacts last produced by the opening process; one package may pin versions from multiple processes in the same project. Epic 4 does not own *when* packages get published or *what goes in them* — that decision lives in downstream process-module epics. What Epic 4 owns is the storage contract, the typed internal mutations that downstream callers use to write to the tables, and the test coverage that proves the contract is correct.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design.md:97:| File content storage | Convex File Storage (`contentStorageId` pointer; Epic 4 relocates the pointer from `artifacts` to the new `artifactVersions` table — see Issues Found) | Epic 3 implementation addendum + Epic 4 storage model change |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design.md:167:Three new Convex tables — `artifactVersions` (one row per durable version of one artifact), `packageSnapshots` (one row per published package), and `packageSnapshotMembers` (many rows per snapshot) — plus a storage model change on the existing `artifacts` table (Epic 3's `contentStorageId` field moves out; this is a schema rewrite, not a data-preserving user-data migration). All three new tables are generic at the platform level: process-type-specific semantics (which artifacts constitute a reviewable package for a `FeatureSpecification` vs. a `FeatureImplementation`) stay in downstream process-module code, not in this schema.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design.md:169:After the migration, `artifacts` carries only project-scoped identity fields: `projectId`, `displayName`, and a new `createdAt` field. Previously-stored `processId`, `contentStorageId`, `currentVersionLabel`, and `updatedAt` are removed. No version-specific state remains on the row, and reviewability is no longer inferred from an artifact-row process attachment.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design.md:171:`artifactVersions` stores `artifactId`, `versionLabel`, `contentStorageId` (the Convex File Storage handle, relocated here from `artifacts`), `contentKind` (`markdown` or `unsupported`), `bytes`, `createdAt`, and `createdByProcessId`. One row per revision; content itself still lives in Convex File Storage. \"Current artifact content\" is the latest row by `createdAt` — a single source of truth, no denormalized field to keep in sync.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design.md:208:A package is a **durable snapshot published from one process review context over a fixed ordered set of artifact versions**. Membership is captured by `packageSnapshotMembers` rows, each of which pins (`packageSnapshotId`, `position`, `artifactId`, `artifactVersionId`). The `(artifactId, artifactVersionId)` pair is the source of truth for what the package contains — revising the artifact later publishes a new `artifactVersions` row, but the snapshot's member row continues pointing at the original version id. Members may pin versions produced by multiple processes in the same project. Snapshots do not mutate.\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design.md:240:| Artifacts | Inherited from platform tech arch + current materials surface | **Schema migration**: `artifacts.contentStorageId` removed; content pointer moves to new `artifactVersions` table. Epic 3's checkpoint writer rewired from overwrite-in-place to append-version-row |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design.md:264:        CONVEX[Convex: artifactVersions,<br/>packageSnapshots, snapshotMembers]\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design.md:332:| `apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts` | MODIFIED | Add reads for `artifactVersions`, `packageSnapshots`, `packageSnapshotMembers`; add `getArtifactVersionContentUrl` helper; add typed internal-mutation wrappers for `insertArtifactVersion` and `publishPackageSnapshot` | AC-1 through AC-6 |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design.md:349:| `convex/artifactVersions.ts` | NEW | Durable artifact version rows + typed `internalMutation insertArtifactVersion` + `internalQuery`s for list / get / content-URL | AC-2, AC-6 |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design.md:352:| `convex/artifacts.ts` | **MODIFIED (storage model change)** | Table shape trims to project-scoped artifact identity: `projectId`, `displayName`, and a new `createdAt` field. **Removed fields: `processId`, `contentStorageId`, `currentVersionLabel`, `updatedAt`** — version-specific state relocates to or is derived from `artifactVersions`, and process linkage moves to process-reference / version-provenance surfaces. Epic 3's checkpoint writer path is rewritten to insert a new `artifactVersions` row via `insertArtifactVersion` rather than overwrite in place. Every caller of the removed fields is rewritten to use `getLatestArtifactVersion`. See `tech-design-server.md` §Artifact Storage Model Change for the exact field-by-field delta. | AC-2 |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design.md:353:| `apps/platform/server/services/processes/readers/materials-section.reader.ts` | MODIFIED | Artifact summary read-path rewrite: per-artifact projections now co-query `artifactVersions` to derive `currentVersionLabel` (from latest `versionLabel`) and `updatedAt` (from latest `createdAt`, fallback to `artifacts.createdAt`). `ArtifactSummary` schema is unchanged; derivation changes | AC-2 |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design.md:354:| `convex/schema.ts` | MODIFIED | Remove `contentStorageId` from `artifacts` validator; add `artifactVersions`, `packageSnapshots`, `packageSnapshotMembers` tables + indexes | AC-2, AC-4 |\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design.md:390:│   │   └── platform-store.ts                      # MODIFIED (add artifactVersions + packageSnapshots reads; add content-URL helper; add insertArtifactVersion + publishPackageSnapshot wrappers)\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design.md:394:│   │       └── materials-section.reader.ts        # MODIFIED (artifact summary derives currentVersionLabel + updatedAt from artifactVersions)\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design.md:441:├── artifacts.ts                                   # MODIFIED (project-scoped identity: projectId/displayName/createdAt; processId/contentStorageId/currentVersionLabel/updatedAt removed)\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design.md:442:├── artifactVersions.ts                            # NEW (table + typed insertArtifactVersion + list/get/content-URL)\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design.md:476:        TABLES[artifactVersions,<br/>packageSnapshots,<br/>packageSnapshotMembers]\ndocs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design.md:523:| Chunk 0 | Foundation: monorepo wiring (`pnpm-workspace.yaml`, root `package.json`, root tsconfig), workspace package scaffold with build/test/typecheck scripts, shared contracts, Convex storage model change on `artifacts` (remove `processId`, `content