n124:## Browser API Layer\\n128:### `apps/platform/client/browser-api/process-work-surface-api.ts`\\n136:export async function startProcess(args: {\\n141:export async function resumeProcess(args: {\\n157:### `apps/platform/client/browser-api/process-live-transport.ts`\\n171:This module wraps the browser `WebSocket` API. The page and store consume typed\\n174:## Feature File Layout\\n190:### Module Responsibility Matrix\\n194:| `app/router.ts` | MODIFIED | Add process-work-surface route parsing and navigation helpers | shared contracts | AC-1.1, AC-6.1, AC-6.4 |\\n195:| `app/store.ts` | MODIFIED | Hold durable process-surface state and live transport metadata | shared contracts | AC-1.4, AC-2.2, AC-3.6, AC-6.x |\\n198:| `process-work-surface-page.ts` | NEW | Route-driven bootstrap, live subscription lifecycle, action orchestration, section rendering | store, HTTP API, live transport, process feature modules | AC-1.1 to AC-6.6 |\\n203:| `process-response-composer.ts` | NEW | Submit responses, block invalid submits, surface in-session validation state | process API, store | AC-3.1 to AC-3.6 |\\n204:| `process-live-status.ts` | NEW | Show connected/disconnected/reconnecting state and retry path | store | AC-6.2, AC-6.5 |\\n206:## Flow 1: Route Entry and Durable Process Surface Bootstrap\\n212:dedicated work surface. The page needs to resolve the route, fetch the durable\\n217:    participant Router as router.ts\\n220:    participant Store as store.ts\\n236:| Route parsing support | `apps/platform/client/app/router.ts` | `export function parseRoute(url: URL): ParsedRoute { throw new NotImplementedError('parseRoute') }` |\\n244:| TC-1.1a | open process from project shell | `tests/service/client/process-router.test.ts` | Start on project shell, activate open-process action | Router navigates to dedicated process route |\\n245:| TC-1.1b | direct process URL opens surface | `tests/service/client/process-router.test.ts` | Initial route is process route | Process surface page mounts and fetches bootstrap |\\n251:| TC-6.1a | browser reload restores process surface | `tests/service/client/process-router.test.ts` | Reload current process route | Same route and bootstrap fetch restored |\\n252:| TC-6.1b | return later restores visible state | `tests/integration/process-work-surface.test.ts` | Reopen process route in fresh session | Latest durable process surface visible |\\n253:| TC-6.4a | missing process shows unavailable state | `tests/service/client/process-router.test.ts` | Route loads with `PROCESS_NOT_FOUND` | Unavailable state rendered |\\n254:| TC-6.4b | revoked access blocks process surface | `tests/service/client/process-router.test.ts` | Route loads with forbidden response | Access-denied state rendered |\\n256:## Flow 2: Start and Resume Actions With Same-Session Updates\\n258:**Covers:** AC-2.1, AC-2.4, AC-2.5\\n260:Start and resume are not just mutations; they are the first moment where the\\n270:    participant Store as store.ts\\n273:    Note over User,Page: AC-2.1: start or resume available process\\n275:    Page->>Api: startProcess() / resumeProcess()\\n278:    Note over Page,Store: AC-2.5: same-session update\\n293:| Start action API client | `apps/platform/client/browser-api/process-work-surface-api.ts` | `export async function startProcess(): Promise<StartProcessResponse> { throw new NotImplementedError('startProcess') }` |\\n294:| Resume action API client | `apps/platform/client/browser-api/process-work-surface-api.ts` | `export async function resumeProcess(): Promise<ResumeProcessResponse> { throw new NotImplementedError('resumeProcess') }` |\\n300:| TC-2.1a | start draft process | `tests/service/client/process-work-surface-page.test.ts` | Draft process bootstrap + start action | Process state changes in-session |\\n301:| TC-2.1b | resume paused process | `tests/service/client/process-work-surface-page.test.ts` | Paused process bootstrap + resume action | Process state changes in-session |\\n302:| TC-2.1c | resume inte