odyStatus: 'error',\n   319\t      bodyError: {\n   320\t        code: 'REVIEW_RENDER_FAILED',\n   321\t        message,\n   322\t      },\n   323\t      createdAt: version.createdAt,\n   324\t      producedByProcessId: version.createdByProcessId,\n   325\t      producedByProcessDisplayLabel,\n   326\t    };\n   327\t  }\n   328\t}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_63","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/stories/02-versioned-checkpoint-realignment.md | sed -n '30,120p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_63","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/stories/02-versioned-checkpoint-realignment.md | sed -n '30,120p'\"","aggregated_output":"    30\t\n    31\t- Review workspace eligibility\n    32\t- Package publication and package context\n    33\t- Degraded-state recovery behavior\n    34\t\n    35\t**Dependencies**\n    36\t\n    37\t- Story 0 foundation\n    38\t- Story 1 project artifact association without process ownership\n    39\t- Existing artifact checkpoint path from Epic 3\n    40\t- [tech-design.md](../tech-design.md), [tech-design-server.md](../tech-design-server.md), [tech-design-client.md](../tech-design-client.md)\n    41\t- [test-plan.md](../test-plan.md)\n    42\t\n    43\t### Acceptance Criteria\n    44\t<!-- Jira: Acceptance Criteria field -->\n    45\t**AC-2.1:** When a process revises an existing project artifact, the system creates a new version instead of transferring artifact ownership to the revising process.\n    46\t\n    47\t- **TC-2.1a: New revision becomes new version**\n    48\t  - Given: A process revises an existing artifact\n    49\t  - When: Checkpointed artifact output is persisted\n    50\t  - Then: A new artifact version is created for the same artifact\n    51\t- **TC-2.1b: Artifact is not reassigned to one primary process**\n    52\t  - Given: An artifact already has history from an earlier process\n    53\t  - When: A later process persists a new version\n    54\t  - Then: The artifact is not rewritten as if it now belongs only to the later process\n    55\t\n    56\t**AC-2.2:** Version-level provenance identifies which process produced each artifact revision.\n    57\t\n    58\t- **TC-2.2a: Producing process recorded on version**\n    59\t  - Given: A new artifact version is created\n    60\t  - When: Version provenance is read later\n    61\t  - Then: The producing process for that version is visible\n    62\t- **TC-2.2b: Earlier version provenance remains readable**\n    63\t  - Given: An artifact has versions produced by multiple processes\n    64\t  - When: Earlier versions are reviewed\n    65\t  - Then: Each earlier version still shows the process that produced it\n    66\t\n    67\t**AC-2.3:** Current artifact summaries resolve the latest version correctly after multi-process revision history.\n    68\t\n    69\t- **TC-2.3a: Latest version shown after later process revision**\n    70\t  - Given: A later process created a new artifact version\n    71\t  - When: Current artifact summaries are loaded\n    72\t  - Then: The summaries show the latest current version label and update time\n    73\t- **TC-2.3b: Earlier versions remain reviewable**\n    74\t  - Given: An artifact has more than one version\n    75\t  - When: The user opens artifact review\n    76\t  - Then: Earlier versions remain available for selection and review\n    77\t\n    78\t### Technical Design\n    79\t<!-- Jira: Technical Notes or sub-section of Description -->\n    80\tThis story owns the write-path flip from artifact-row ownership semantics to version-row provenance semantics.\n    81\t\n    82\t#### Endpoints Affected By Read Model\n    83\t\n    84\t| Operation | Method | Path | Description |\n    85\t|---|---|---|---|\n    86\t| Get project shell | `GET` | `/api/projects/{projectId}` | Returns project-level artifact state with project-scoped artifact identity and latest version summary |\n    87\t| Get process work surface | `GET` | `/api/projects/{projectId}/processes/{processId}` | Returns process-local current artifact materials and current outputs without implying artifact ownership |\n    88\t| Get artifact review target | `GET` | `/api/projects/{projectId}/processes/{processId}/review/artifacts/{artifactId}` | Returns one artifact's version list and selected review state for that process context |\n    89\t\n    90\t#### Artifact Version Summary\n    91\t\n    92\t| Field | Type | Required | Validation | Description |\n    93\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n    94\t| `versionId` | string | yes | non-empty | Stable artifact version identifier |\n    95\t| `versionLabel` | string | yes | non-empty | User-visible version label |\n    96\t| `createdAt` | timestamp | yes | ISO 8601 UTC | Version creation timestamp |\n    97\t| `producedByProcessId` | string | yes | non-empty | Process that created this version |\n    98\t| `producedByProcessDisplayLabel` | string | no | non-empty when present | User-facing producing-process label |\n    99\t\n   100\t#### Project Artifact Summary\n   101\t\n   102\t| Field | Type | Required | Validation | Description |\n   103\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n   104\t| `artifactId` | string | yes | non-empty | Stable artifact identifier |\n   105\t| `displayName` | string | yes | non-empty | Human-readable artifact name |\n   106\t| `currentVersionLabel` | string | no | non-empty when present | Latest current version label |\n   107\t| `updatedAt` | timestamp | yes | ISO 8601 UTC | Latest durable update time for this artifact |\n   108\t\n   109\tImplementation notes:\n   110\t\n   111\t- `artifacts` keeps project-scoped identity only\n   112\t- each checkpointed revision inserts a new `artifactVersions` row\n   113\t- latest-version summary fields are derived from the newest durable version, not from artifact ownership metadata\n   114\t\n   115\tSee the tech design document for full architecture, implementation targets, and test mapping.\n   116\t\n   117\t### Definition of Done\n   118\t<!-- Jira: Definition of Done or Acceptance Criteria footer -->\n   119\t- Revising an existing project artifact creates a new version without reassigning the artifact\n   120\t- Version rows preserve producing-process provenance across multi-process histories\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
