{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_70","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/tech-design-client.md | sed -n '330,410p'\"","aggregated_output":"   330\t- selected version label\n   331\t- version switcher\n   332\t- unsupported fallback\n   333\t- markdown body\n   334\t\n   335\tEpic 5 changes the messaging more than the structure:\n   336\t\n   337\t- zero-version empty state becomes \"This artifact exists in the current process\n   338\t  context but has no durable version yet.\"\n   339\t- unavailable-version messaging should mention version availability, not\n   340\t  process mismatch\n   341\t- current version label remains a projection of the latest durable version, not\n   342\t  an ownership marker\n   343\t- selected-version metadata and version-switcher rows expose\n   344\t  `producedByProcessId` and `producedByProcessDisplayLabel` so the producing\n   345\t  process remains visible in the review experience\n   346\t\n   347\t### `package-review-panel.ts`\n   348\t\n   349\tThis panel already renders:\n   350\t\n   351\t- package identity and type\n   352\t- member nav\n   353\t- selected-member subpanel\n   354\t- export trigger\n   355\t\n   356\tEpic 5 keeps that structure and changes the interpretation:\n   357\t\n   358\t- selected member failure messages refer to unavailable pinned versions\n   359\t- mixed-producer members are normal\n   360\t- fully degraded published packages still remain targetable so reopen and\n   361\t  provenance inspection remain possible\n   362\t- exportability is still server-driven, but the client copy should explain\n   363\t  \"One or more pinned members are unavailable\" rather than \"This package is not\n   364\t  owned by the current process\"\n   365\t\n   366\t## Interface Definitions\n   367\t\n   368\t### Project Artifact Summary\n   369\t\n   370\t```ts\n   371\texport interface ArtifactSummary {\n   372\t  artifactId: string;\n   373\t  displayName: string;\n   374\t  currentVersionLabel: string | null;\n   375\t  updatedAt: string;\n   376\t}\n   377\t```\n   378\t\n   379\t### Review Version Contracts\n   380\t\n   381\t```ts\n   382\texport interface ArtifactVersionSummary {\n   383\t  versionId: string;\n   384\t  versionLabel: string;\n   385\t  isCurrent: boolean;\n   386\t  createdAt: string;\n   387\t  producedByProcessId: string;\n   388\t  producedByProcessDisplayLabel: string | null;\n   389\t}\n   390\t\n   391\texport interface ArtifactVersionDetail extends ArtifactVersionSummary {\n   392\t  contentKind: 'markdown' | 'unsupported';\n   393\t  bodyStatus?: 'ready' | 'error';\n   394\t  body?: string;\n   395\t  bodyError?: ReviewTargetError;\n   396\t  mermaidBlocks?: MermaidBlock[];\n   397\t}\n   398\t```\n   399\t\n   400\tClient consequences:\n   401\t\n   402\t- `version-switcher.ts` can keep its current listbox structure, but its row\n   403\t  metadata should include the producing process display label, falling back to\n   404\t  the id only when no display label can be resolved\n   405\t- `artifact-review-panel.ts` should render the selected version's producing\n   406\t  process display label beside the created timestamp, again falling back to the\n   407\t  id only when needed\n   408\t- package-member artifact panels inherit that same provenance field through the\n   409\t  pinned artifact review payload\n   410\t\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_71","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"artifactsRead\":[\"convex/_generated/ai/guidelines.md\",\"docs/onboarding/current-state-index.md\",\"docs/onboarding/current-state-project-and-process-shell.md\",\"docs/onboarding/current-state-process-work-surface.md\",\"docs/onboarding/current-state-tech-design.md\",\"docs/onboarding/current-state-code-map.md\",\"docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/stories/02-versioned-checkpoint-realignment.md\",\"docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/tech-design.md\",\"docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/tech-design-server.md\",\"docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/tech-design-client.md\",\"docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/test-plan.md\",\"convex/schema.ts\",\"convex/artifacts.ts\",\"convex/artifacts.test.ts\",\"apps/platform/shared/contracts/schemas.ts\",\"apps/platform/shared/contracts/review-workspace.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/projects/readers/artifact-section.reader.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/processes/readers/materials-section.reader.ts\",\"apps/platform/server/services/review/artifact-review.service.ts\",\"apps/platform/client/features/projects/artifact-section.ts\",\"apps/platform/client/features/review/artifact-review-panel.ts\",\"apps/platform/client/features/review/version-switcher.ts\",\"tests/service/server/project-shell-bootstrap-api.test.ts\",\"tests/service/server/artifact-review-api.test.ts\",\"tests/service/server/process-work-surface-api.test.ts\",\"tests/service/client/artifact-review-panel.test.ts\",\"tests/service/client/version-switcher.test.ts\",\"tests/integration/review-workspace.test.ts\"],\"reviewScopeSummary\":\"Read the Story 2 spec plus the full Epic 5 tech-design/test-plan set, then verified the checkpoint write path, latest-version summary projections, artifact review provenance payloads, and the shipped review UI/client coverage for Versioned Checkpoint Realignment.\",\"priorFindingStatuses\":[],\"newFindings\":[{\"id\":\"SV-02-001\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Review UI never surfaces the producing-process provenance that Story 2 adds to artifact versions\",\"evidence\":\"Story 2 defines `producedByProcessId` and `producedByProcessDisplayLabel` as the version-provenance fields that make the producing process visible later (docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/stories/02-versioned-checkpoint-realignment.md:56-98), and the client design says selected-version metadata and version-switcher rows must expose them (docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/tech-design-client.md:343-345,402-407). The server now populates both fields on every version summary and selected-version detail (apps/platform/server/services/review/artifact-review.service.ts:141-165,205-326), but the shipped review UI never reads either field: apps/platform/client/features/review/artifact-review-panel.ts:28-106 renders only artifact/version labels and createdAt, and apps/platform/client/features/review/version-switcher.ts:25-109 renders only versionLabel/current/selected plus createdAt. A repo-wide search found no production client consumer of `producedByProcessId` or `producedByProcessDisplayLabel` under apps/platform/client/features, so a user reviewing earlier revisions still cannot see which process produced each version.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/client/features/review/artifact-review-panel.ts\",\"apps/platform/client/features/review/version-switcher.ts\",\"tests/service/client/artifact-review-panel.test.ts\",\"tests/service/client/version-switcher.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-2.2\",\"TC-2.2a\",\"TC-2.2b\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"same-session-implementor\",\"blocking\":true}],\"openFindings\":[{\"id\":\"SV-02-001\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Review UI never surfaces the producing-process provenance that Story 2 adds to artifact versions\",\"evidence\":\"Story 2 defines `producedByProcessId` and `producedByProcessDisplayLabel` as the version-provenance fields that make the producing process visible later (docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/stories/02-versioned-checkpoint-realignment.md:56-98), and the client design says selected-version metadata and version-switcher rows must expose them (docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/tech-design-client.md:343-345,402-407). The server now populates both fields on every version summary and selected-version detail (apps/platform/server/services/review/artifact-review.service.ts:141-165,205-326), but the shipped review UI never reads either field: apps/platform/client/features/review/artifact-review-panel.ts:28-106 renders only artifact/version labels and createdAt, and apps/platform/client/features/review/version-switcher.ts:25-109 renders only versionLabel/current/selected plus createdAt. A repo-wide search found no production client consumer of `producedByProcessId` or `producedByProcessDisplayLabel` under apps/platform/client/features, so a user reviewing earlier revisions still cannot see which process produced each version.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"apps/platform/client/features/review/artifact-review-panel.ts\",\"apps/platform/client/features/review/version-switcher.ts\",\"tests/service/client/artifact-review-panel.test.ts\",\"tests/service/client/version-switcher.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-2.2\",\"TC-2.2a\",\"TC-2.2b\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"same-session-implementor\",\"blocking\":true}],\"requirementCoverage\":{\"verified\":[\"AC-2.1\",\"TC-2.1a\",\"TC-2.1b\",\"AC-2.3\",\"TC-2.3a\",\"TC-2.3b\"],\"unverified\":[\"AC-2.2\",\"TC-2.2a\",\"TC-2.2b\"]},\"gatesRun\":[{\"command\":\"corepack pnpm exec vitest run convex/artifacts.test.ts tests/service/server/project-shell-bootstrap-api.test.ts tests/service/server/artifact-review-api.test.ts tests/service/server/process-work-surface-api.test.ts --environment node\",\"result\":\"pass\"},{\"command\":\"corepack pnpm exec vitest run tests/service/client/artifact-review-panel.test.ts tests/service/client/version-switcher.test.ts --environment jsdom\",\"result\":\"pass\"},{\"command\":\"corepack pnpm run green-verify\",\"result\":\"pass\"},{\"command\":\"corepack pnpm run verify-all\",\"result\":\"pass\"}],\"mockOrShimAuditFindings\":[\"No production-path mocks, shims, or fake adapters were found in the reviewed Story 2 runtime paths; the Convex-backed implementation uses real store/query surfaces.\",\"Test-only shim note: InMemoryPlatformStore still fabricates a synthetic artifact version from legacy artifact-summary fields when no explicit version rows are seeded (apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts:2965-2990). That behavior is limited to tests/in-memory flows, but it can hide provenance regressions if fixtures omit `artifactVersionsByArtifactId`.\"],\"recommendedNextStep\":\"revise\",\"recommendedFixScope\":\"same-session-implementor\",\"openQuestions\":[],\"additionalObservations\":[\"AC-2.1 and AC-2.3 are otherwise in good shape: convex/artifacts.ts:22-26 and 401-429 keep artifact identity project-scoped while appending new version rows, and convex/artifacts.ts:46-70 plus apps/platform/server/services/processes/readers/materials-section.reader.ts:19-50 make both project-shell and process-material reads consume latest-version projections.\",\"`verify-all` passed, but the `test:e2e` lane is still scaffold-only and prints a skip message, so there is no browser-automation proof for the Story 2 review flow.\"]}"}}
